WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.180
Good work at the student assembly.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.470
Yeah. I heard you were watching?

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.870
It felt like I was there.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.680
The people here can do anything, huh?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.790
Hey, did Chiaki and Kamiya-san 
have an agreement in advance?

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.730
I heard later...

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.410
Give me an alternate proposal.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.090
That's right!

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.000
I'm hurt!

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:39.840
Apologize!

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.840
<i>So that's what he meant...</i>

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.520
<i>All right!</i>

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.730
An alternate proposal?

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.740
Yeah.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.360
That was enough to get things to a 
conclusion everyone could accept.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.770
They're both amazing, huh?

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.410
Yeah.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.930
You have many talented people around you.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.450
Hey, what are you thinking?

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:39.380
<b>Twenty-third Haunting 
Do You Like Other Faces? Or Not?</b>

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.530
Well, now we can focus on 
preparations for the culture fair.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.420
That time already?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.080
You want to know what a culture fair is?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.230
It's like a festival.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.570
Fes-ti-val.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.140
Festival!

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.890
That scared me.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.560
Um...

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.010
We heard there's a festival, chirp.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.250
When, chirp?

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.690
Where, chirp?

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.280
A festival?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.660
If there's a festival, we'd better be there.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.520
No, it's just a culture fair.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.910
A culture fair, huh?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.970
Feels like youth!

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.420
Brings back memories...

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.790
When I remember those days,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.210
the taste of blood spreads through my mouth.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.120
So, Yushi-kun, when's the culture fair?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.090
Well...

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.870
Oh, my. Evidently, everyone is 
curious about the culture fair.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.830
Yeah, they are.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.390
<b>Ten Days Until the Culture Fair!</b>

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.390
<i>Anyway, preparations for 
the culture fair began.</i>

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.680
Our class exhibit was...

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.780
Don't move.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.200
<b>Oni-Hunting Game 
1:  Try    Yen</b>

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.200
An oni-hunting game, where you 
throw balls at oni.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.000
<i>An oni mask, huh?</i>

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.800
<i>I've seen the real thing at the apartments.</i>

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.990
What's this?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.880
An alien?

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.950
Make sure it looks like an oni.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.000
It really is an oni.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.870
Chiaki isn't here again today.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.180
He said he was respecting our independence,

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.020
but he's probably somewhere, slacking off.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.950
He gets paid anyway, right?

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.430
Lucky guy.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.670
Those guys...

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.340
Ignore them.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.600
But...

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.260
It's frustrating for us, too.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.040
Sorry.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.780
Anyway!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.140
Forget the mask, and let's dress you up!

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.690
You should have done
that in the first place...

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.460
<b>Yamamoto</b>

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.380
<b>The Darling</b>

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.580
What's wrong?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.770
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.870
Next, time to get ready for the club exhibit.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.460
We'll be so busy!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.250
You look like you're having fun, though.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.110
Yeah.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.320
I love this festival!

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.450
Tashiro. Inaba.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.070
Kamiya-san!

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:21.330
I know you're busy, but can we talk?

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.300
Since the assembly,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.130
reaction against Chiaki-sensei 
has been growing, right?

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.060
Yes.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:37.500
There are even kids in our class 
who don't like him anymore.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:42.810
After the cheating, it was decided that 
all cell phones would be banned.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.560
It was?

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:45.430
Yes.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.950
Aoki-sensei, for example,

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.060
said the teachers should follow 
the principal's decision.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.790
Yeah, I can see that.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.790
But Chiaki-sensei...

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.330
That won't solve anything.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.190
Leave it to me.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:01.830
So he asked to have a student assembly.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.920
I see...

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:08.840
For our sake, he volunteered 
to be the bad guy.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.230
That's pretty frustrating.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.860
Yeah, for me, too.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.450
They all loved him

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.980
until he did one thing they didn't 
like, and now they all hate him.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.490
I'll just say it. I hate people like that.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.180
I understand!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.700
What do we do?

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.930
I want to repay him.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.810
Egami told me about you.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.000
Find some information about 
Chiaki-sensei, right away.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.910
The more sensational, the better.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.290
You know what I mean, right?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.750
Leave it to me.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.990
I'm counting on you.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.770
That was...

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.850
amazingly manly.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.600
Kamiya-san's so cool!

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.520
I'm in love!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.130
You gonna be okay?

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.120
You have to get ready for the festival.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.790
Did you think I hadn't already 
looked into Chiaki-chan?

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.270
Always save your trump 
card for last, Inaba-kun!

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.230
Wait! What are you doing?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.910
Don't worry! Just what Kamiya-san said to!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.190
That's not it!

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.940
I mean don't do anything bad, 
socially or ethically!

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.520
Ha ha ha!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.920
What is she planning?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.930
I'm back.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.000
Welcome back!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.510
Mariko-san! Hi, there...

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.600
I'm Sailor Mariko!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:44.610
What do you think?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.590
I have a collection of all the sailor 
uniforms from across space and time.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.280
Have a look.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.740
Antiquary! You're okay?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.790
With what?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.710
Um, well...

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.750
Weren't you fighting someone, somewhere?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.770
Oh, I probably should've left that alone.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.420
I always wonder where you get all this stuff!

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:18.390
This is the same one I had 
when I was in high school!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.610
I remember this!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.520
I've never worn a school uniform.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.940
Is this too short?

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:26.730
We've still got it, huh?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.330
Y-Yeah...

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.930
Everyone's in a culture fair mood, huh?

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.890
That doesn't mean they have to wear uniforms.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:38.290
I'm going to eat.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.720
Et tu, Ruriko-san?

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.160
<b>Takoyaki          Yakisoba          Yakitori</b>

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.780
The takoyaki is so good, chirp.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:46.450
So is the yakisoba, chirp!

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.330
So is the yakitori, chirp.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:48.960
Eh?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.760
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.590
<b>Nine Days Left!</b>

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.070
Hey, want to ask Yamamoto-san to join?

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.910
Shh! No way!

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:03.960
Yeah.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.680
She'd say, "Why do I have to do 
something as rudimentary as this?"

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.530
Why is she even here?

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.660
<i>Why do I have to hear things like that?</i>

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.240
<i>You're in the way...</i>

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.880
<i>All of you!</i>

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.330
On to the next scene, okay?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.760
Where the female pirate, Panna Cotta,

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:39.930
saves her partner, Nata de Coco, 
from the enemy.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.080
Okay!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.350
Got it!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.070
Sound effects, ready?

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.430
Looking good!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.920
<i>What is that? A school play?</i>

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:54.940
Hey, can we say "Keep holding 
my hand," for, "Don't let go"?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.780
I'm not sure...

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.930
Wait, I'll look it up.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.280
<i>You don't even know that?</i>

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.010
<i>Fine, I'll tell you.</i>

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:08.240
"Don't let go."

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:12.560
We want to keep it tense, 
so no long sentences.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:14.580
Let's use, "Don't let go!"

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:15.900
Got it!

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.690
You're so smart, president!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.130
What's up?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.230
Just now... I thought I saw Yamamoto.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.600
Konacchan?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.520
She isn't here.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.020
I'll go take a look.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.960
<i>Did I imagine it?</i>

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:39.940
There she is.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:40.950
Yamamoto!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.360
Inaba-kun, no running in the hall.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:48.040
<b>Members Wanted</b>

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.300
Right.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.030
Perfect. Can we talk?

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.400
No, I'm in a hurry.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.920
Don't worry. It won't take long.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.840
O-Okay...

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.260
What is it?

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:59.010
Have you been having any problems lately?

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:03.240
It must be hard without your parents 
when you're all by yourself,

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.600
but don't push yourself.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:08.140
I'm on your side, all right?

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.580
<i>You don't have to tell me that now!</i>

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.420
<b>Eight Days Left!</b>

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.650
I can't take any more...

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:55.690
The club president and Tashiro 
are both overworking me.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.510
I'm going to take a break.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.210
Chiaki...

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.780
Inaba?

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.560
What, slacking off?

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.190
You're one to talk.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.560
How has it been lately?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.620
You're so lazy.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.320
Well, I'm doing okay, I guess.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.580
Glad to hear it. Good luck.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.580
Come by the classroom, once in a while.

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.820
You guys will be fine without me.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.750
I thought you'd say that.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:29.980
Chiaki, what did you do at your culture fair?

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:32.840
Hmm, what did I do?

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:34.260
You don't remember?

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:36.870
I'm the type who doesn't focus on the past.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.820
Sure you aren't going senile?

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.640
I'll see you later, behind the building.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.770
Sorry, seriously.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.200
I won't forgive you.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:46.930
Whatever happened to her?

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.110
Her?

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:52.290
You know, that girl who wasn't 
getting along with your club?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.960
Oh... Yamamoto?

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.890
It isn't going well?

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.310
It's just tough.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.130
Don't whine.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.050
I'm not whining.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.610
I'm heading back.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:19.850
What about you?

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.930
I'll get a bit more fresh air.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.090
Don't slack off too much.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.740
You're one to talk.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:27.820
Right?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.330
This is that...

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.420
What?

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.170
Hey!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.520
Please! Don't move!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.230
<i>I was able to take the damage 
from Tashiro's wounds,</i>

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.360
<i>so it didn't become the worst-case scenario.</i>

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.690
Inaba...

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:06.780
Just be quiet.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.480
<i>Move the damage...</i>

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:15.110
<i>Looking good.</i>

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.840
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.460
<i>Just a little more...</i>

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.660
<i>A little more!</i>

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:36.230
Why are you panting in front of me?

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:40.320
U-Uh, I'm not doing anything weird!

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.230
What do you mean by weird?

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:47.070
My body suddenly feels lighter.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.840
What did you do?

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:52.640
Sh-Shiatsu massage!

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.110
You're a strange guy.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.790
Anyway, is something wrong with you?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.710
Well, it's nothing bad.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.220
Thin blood?

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.380
My red blood cell count is low.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:18.140
They call it anemia.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:19.570
Anemia...

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.950
Then that medicine...

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:28.060
So why do you smoke?

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:30.970
The cigarettes won't let me quit them.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.320
What?

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.920
My last job was pretty rough,

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:38.020
so after I quit, I was gonna take a year off.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.270
But I was called here very suddenly.

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:44.670
I see. Because Hayasaka-sensei 
was hospitalized.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.560
In the end, I only had six months off.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.140
They're really harsh on me.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.350
But due to that, I met 
an interesting student.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:54.670
Chiaki...

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:10.220
<i>Chiaki may really be pushing himself hard.</i>

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.890
Splendid work back there!

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:13.660
Fool!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.680
You saved someone with your power!

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.780
As your servant, I am very proud.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.440
That's an exaggeration.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.130
But yeah.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.270
If I helped Chiaki, even a little, I'm happy.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:27.210
Of course!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.400
I've grown up, too!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.990
I was able to transfer the damage 
without Akine-chan's help!

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.400
Oh, that was by chance.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.770
You could not have done 
that with just anyone.

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:38.880
What?

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.880
Don't lift me up just to kick me down.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:45.730
Your bodies are probably very compatible!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.520
Don't make it sound weird.

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:50.260
I was able to save Chiaki with this hand.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.760
Let me be a little proud...

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.460
Okay, you're fine now.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.460
Thank you.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.770
Um, I...

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:15.980
I heard you took someone's damage.

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:19.210
That's right! I was able to do it myself!

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:19.970
Yeah.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.100
Be careful next time.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.050
Depending on the amount of damage,

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:28.160
you could pass out, like you 
just did, or even die.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:31.470
Okay...

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:33.420
This was a rare case.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:37.760
Your bodies were very compatible, 
so by chance, you were able to do it.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:38.980
Don't be arrogant.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.640
I'm sorry.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.220
Just as I said, yes?

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:44.580
Shut up.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.470
The damage is gone now, right?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.320
Then...

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:52.590
Let's eat!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.600
Modorigatsuo sashimi!

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.510
Let's eat!

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.420
It's so fatty, like toro!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:08.900
I love katsuo tuna, too.

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:15.870
What excellent harmony with the condiments!

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:19.360
It goes perfectly with Japanese sake.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:23.540
These mushrooms and gizzards 
go great with sake.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.950
I love it.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.820
Yeah, the mushrooms are so crispy, 
and the gizzards are so chewy...

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:31.350
This is olive oil, huh?

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:32.790
Healthy!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.390
<i>Even ghosts care about their health?</i>

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:44.520
Thin blood, huh?

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.160
A friend of mine has that.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.500
Usually, women get it.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.730
Really?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.240
Yeah, when I was a student,

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:57.070
my periods were so bad, I couldn't stand.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:58.860
Hey, stop that.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.570
I've got pretty high blood pressure.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:06.190
It's hard to even imagine 
you tired from anemia!

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.580
I'll exorcise you.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.890
Sorry!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.810
Anemia can't be cured with 
blood transfusions.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.890
So the most you can do is take medicine.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.800
I see.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:26.310
Supposedly, you get used to it, though.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:30.380
But it can be bad enough to cause a coma.

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.150
So it really is scary.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:35.300
Anemia can put you into a coma?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:39.790
If, for some reason, the brain 
doesn't get enough blood,

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:42.110
it will shut down.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:45.190
Makes sense, if you lack oxygen, right?

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.530
And then the heart stops, as well.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.730
The heart, too?

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:54.190
And then you can fall into a coma and die.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.960
It's called cerebral anemia.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.560
Scary.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:01.260
Sometimes you pass out in judo, right?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.140
It's due to lack of oxygen in the brain.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.400
So you need to fire yourself up 
and wake up, or it's bad.

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:11.480
The brain's delicate, right?

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.820
Your stomach's made of steel, though, huh?

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.390
Sorry!

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.480
If you have trouble with 
illness, I've got this!

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.190
Mt. Hourai's secret medicine,

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:26.760
which China's first emperor 
sought and never got.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:29.660
One sip will make you immortal.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.380
Take a drink, then.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:43.000
Anyway, it seems you have some karmic 
connection with Chiaki-sensei.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.350
Do... I?

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.270
It just happened to go well.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.470
Exactly opposite.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:53.030
It went well because of that connection.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:55.610
You've trained hard every day,

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:58.970
and that connection was there, 
and a miracle occurred.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:02.410
A miracle? It wasn't that big a deal.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.660
But I like the thought.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.270
A karmic connection, huh?

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:12.700
And your bodies were very compatible, too.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.370
You ruined it!

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.300
<i>These drunk adults...</i>

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.540
Laugh all you like, damn it!

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.470
He got mad!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:29.050
<i>I decided to simply be happy 
that I could save Chiaki,</i>

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.140
<i>and that I had a connection with him.</i>

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.500
Idiots. Idiots.

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.870
They're all idiots.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:36.850
All of them.

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:40.250
Why do I have to...

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:13.280
The culture fair's beginning.

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:15.380
We've made it, so nothing 
to worry about, right?

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:16.570
Don't lower your guard.

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:18.910
Accidents are most likely to happen now.

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:21.080
There's a big problem!

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:22.070
What's wrong?

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:25.480
The snacks I was saving are passed 
their expiration date!

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:27.000
Your life's peaceful, huh?

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:30.760
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.470
The Storm Before the Storm.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.850
<b>Twenty-fourth Haunting 
The Storm Before the Storm</b>

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:35.880
No... Don't die, Chiaki!
